<title>USA: Ciatti's Inc note offer becomes affective.</title>
<headline>Ciatti's Inc note offer becomes affective.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ciatti's Inc said Monday its public offering of $2 million principal amount of subordinated notes has become effective with the Securities and Exchange Commission.</p>
<p>The notes mature either one year or three years from the date of issue and pay semi-annual interest of nine percent on one-year notes and 9.25 percent on three-year notes, the restaurant operator said.</p>
<p>The notes are being offered directly by the company and are being offered only to residents of Minnesota.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
